Approved Technology Stack
Frontend:
- React with Vite.
- Modern JavaScript using ES modules.
- Tailwind CSS version 4.
- shadcn/ui.
- React Router.
- Axios.
- TanStack Query.
- Recharts.
- Lucide React.
Backend:
- Node.js.
- Express.js.
- MongoDB.
- Mongoose.
- JWT authentication using HTTP-only cookies.
- bcrypt.
- Zod.
Testing:
- Vitest.
- Supertest.
Development:
- Git and GitHub.
- Postman.
- npm.
Version Management
- Inspect package.json and lockfiles before implementation.
- Use official documentation for installed versions.
- Do not use outdated Tailwind CSS v3 configuration in a v4 project.
- Verify dependency compatibility before installation.
- Record important dependency versions.
- Ask before introducing new libraries or upgrading major versions.
Architecture
- Use a modular monolith.
- Maintain separate client and server applications.
- Use REST APIs for communication.
- Separate HTTP handling from business logic.
- Keep components focused and reusable.
- Prefer readable solutions over unnecessary abstractions.
- Introduce folders and modules when they become necessary.
- Avoid premature optimisation.
Database
- Design schemas according to actual access patterns.
- Explain embedding versus referencing decisions.
- Preserve historical workout data.
- Validate data before persistence.
- Enforce user ownership of private records.
- Store measurement units consistently.
Security
- Never commit secrets or credentials.
- Use environment variables.
- Validate untrusted input.
- Hash passwords securely.
- Protect private endpoints.
- Apply appropriate CSRF, CORS, cookie and rate-limiting protections.
Restrictions
Do not introduce microservices, Redis, Kubernetes, external AI APIs or other infrastructure without a demonstrated need and approval.

Architectural guidelines are boundaries, not instructions for every implementation detail.

Propose improvements when justified.